cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "DiaryPipeline (Notebook Feedback Studio): collecting OneNote diaries and reviewing human-written feedback"
abstract: >-
  A teacher-facing research prototype that reads student diaries from OneNote
  Class Notebooks through Microsoft Graph, parses structured entries and stores
  reviewable snapshots in Firestore. Teachers and interns write feedback; a
  server-side AI reviewer comments on their drafts, with explicit per-comment
  Apply and recorded inputs and outcomes. Human-authored messages are delivered
  through Microsoft Teams or email and retained for inspection and export.
  This release contains the implementation; owner evaluation and
  wider AI-review pilot enablement remain pending.
